Z||000014||rogergarrison||11-12-2001||04:41 PM||||nice job. Cars nice too. make your own dead pedal with flat aluminum plate. You could even drill large holes in a pattern in it. then just screw it in with recessed screws. Make sure you know whats under the screws so you dont hit wires or hoses. Isnt it nice how new carpet makes your car feel new. I got that mirror too, its really nice to keep all those lites behind you dimmed. too bad no one mades outside mirrors like that too.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 11-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||88CoupeV6||11-12-2001||05:06 PM||||Looks nice BAM-BAM, I've been looking at there carpet on ebay and wanted to know how it looks installed. I would love to see how it will look with some type of dead petal. I wonder what type would fit and look good. <P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88coupeV6.jpg">       <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>    <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com/nefa.htm" TARGET=_blank>Join New England Fiero Association</A>||||reg||7
Z||000016||BAM-BAM||11-12-2001||09:44 PM||||Thanks for all the positive comments....<P>Drew- The rear wing is off of a 2000 Mustang, I thought it matched the body lines better than the stock wing. It was easy to layout and install, but I never had a wing in the first place. It might be more of a challenge if you already have holes in the decklid. The car is lowered using Eibach lowering springs and KYB shocks and struts. All of the control arms have Poly bushings installed and new balljoints top and bottom, front and rear. The wheels are Konig Monsoons, 17x7 with Kumho Ecsta tires, 235/45's in the rear and 225/45's in front. I hope that answered your questions.<P>Alex- You are right the carpet is the 80/20 loop. The mats are cut pile. I'll have to get back to you on the carpet code.<P>My7- Yeah I know it looks like an a. It's just the angle and the way the cut pile and the stitching meld. If I brush it back it's clear to see that it is an e.<P>Fieroparts- Don't know just yet Tim, I have still to get everything together. I have been working six tens almost all year and have had very little time to work on anything. I just had to get the carpet in as the road noise was getting to me. Also, I needed to see some progress, however slight it might be. I can't wait to hear that Borla behind the WestCoast headers. Should sound Shweeet!!!! I will let you know as soon as I fire it up. Thanks again for the deal. Yeah I thought T-Tops would look awesome, but I have to wait until I get my fastback. I always thought that a Targa would be the way to go with the notchback. <P>Thanks again guys, I enjoy sharing a little pride!!!!!<P>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||12
